"<b>The great Vishnu temple</b> and the city's landmark — the city is named after it. <i>For those interested:</i> entry is for Hindus only, with a strict traditional dress code (men in a mundu, bare-chested; women in a saree) and no phones inside. Everyone can admire the seven-tiered tower and the old East Fort streets from outside.": "<b>宏伟的毗湿奴神庙</b>，也是这座城市的地标——城市正是以它命名的。<i>有兴趣的朋友请注意：</i>神庙仅限印度教徒入内，着装要求严格遵循传统（男士须穿 mundu 传统围裹布、赤裸上身；女士须穿纱丽），且不得携带手机入内。所有人都可以在外面欣赏七层高的塔楼，以及东堡 (East Fort) 一带的老街。",
