"<a class=\"name-link\" href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Balaramapuram+handloom\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><b>Balaramapuram</b></a> — the handloom village on the way to Kovalam, famous for cream-and-gold <b>kasavu</b> sarees and mundu. <a class=\"inline-link\" href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Balaramapuram+handloom\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open in Google Maps →</a>": "<a class=\"name-link\" href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Balaramapuram+handloom\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><b>巴拉拉马普拉姆 (Balaramapuram)</b></a>——前往科瓦兰 (Kovalam) 途中的手织村落，以米白配金色的<b>kasavu（喀拉拉金边织布）</b>纱丽和 mundu（喀拉拉传统围裹布）闻名。<a class=\"inline-link\" href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Balaramapuram+handloom\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">在 Google Maps 中打开 →</a>",
"<a class=\"name-link\" href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Jayalakshmi+Silks+Thiruvananthapuram\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><b>Jayalakshmi Silks</b></a> — known for traditional Kerala sarees and churidar sets. <a class=\"inline-link\" href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Jayalakshmi+Silks+Thiruvananthapuram\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open in Google Maps →</a>": "<a class=\"name-link\" href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Jayalakshmi+Silks+Thiruvananthapuram\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><b>Jayalakshmi Silks</b></a>——以传统喀拉拉纱丽和 churidar（印度紧身裤套装）闻名。<a class=\"inline-link\" href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Jayalakshmi+Silks+Thiruvananthapuram\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">在 Google Maps 中打开 →</a>",
"It turned out we were both people who liked to leave. Weekends became trailheads and departure gates — helmets and headlamps underground, rice fields glowing outside a wooden window, temple spires on the far horizon. We got lost, got rained on, got hungry, and kept booking the next one. Somewhere in there, going anywhere together stopped being a plan and started being who we are.": "原来，我们都是喜欢出发的人。周末成了步道起点和登机口——戴着头盔和头灯钻进地底，木窗外的稻田泛着光，远方地平线上是寺庙的尖塔。我们迷过路，淋过雨，饿过肚子，却总是接着订下一趟旅程。不知从何时起，一起去往任何地方，不再只是计划，而成了我们本来的样子。",
"A girl from Malaysia. A boy from India. A fintech festival in Singapore that neither of us walked into looking for anything at all. We found each other somewhere between the panels and the coffee queues, and at the end of the night we shook hands. Nobody shakes hands. We both went home knowing something had already started.": "一个来自马来西亚的女孩，一个来自印度的男孩。新加坡的一场金融科技节，我们谁都没想过要在那里遇见什么。却在论坛与排队买咖啡之间找到了彼此；那晚结束时，我们握了握手。没有人会握手的。回家时，我们心里都知道，有些事情已经开始了。",
"<b>From the airport, please use Uber.</b> Download the app before you fly and book your ride once you've collected your bags — the fare is fixed up front and the trip is tracked. If Uber isn't available at the pickup point, use the official <b>prepaid taxi counter</b> inside arrivals rather than drivers who approach you.": "<b>从机场出发，请使用 Uber。</b>请在出发前下载 App，取完行李后再叫车——车费事先固定，行程全程可追踪。如果上车点无法使用 Uber，请前往到达大厅内的官方<b>预付费出租车柜台</b>，不要搭乘主动上前招揽的司机。",
"Mid-January is one of the best times to visit — <b>dry and sunny</b>, around <b>23°C at night</b> and <b>31–32°C during the day</b>, and humid. Rain is rare at this time of year. Pack light, breathable clothes (cotton and linen), sunglasses, a hat and sunscreen; a light shawl is handy for air-conditioned rooms.": "一月中旬是到访的最佳时节之一——<b>干燥晴朗</b>，气温<b>夜间约23°C</b>、<b>白天约31–32°C</b>，较为潮湿。这个季节很少下雨。请携带轻便透气的衣物（棉麻质地）、太阳镜、帽子和防晒霜；带一条薄披肩，在空调房里很实用。",
"If you'd like to mark the occasion, an <b>ang pow</b> — the red envelope given in Malaysia to wish a couple a blessed start — is warmly welcomed. You'll find the ang pow box at the reception entrance, or you're welcome to hand it to any member of our wedding party on the night.": "如您想表达心意，<b>红包 (ang pow)</b>——在马来西亚，人们以这个红色信封祝福新人美满开始——我们衷心欢迎。婚宴入口处设有红包箱，当晚您也可以交给我们婚礼团队的任何一位成员。",
"<b>Emergency numbers</b> (free from any phone in India): <span class=\"sos-grid\"> <span><b>112</b>All emergencies</span> <span><b>100</b>Police</span> <span><b>108</b>Ambulance</span> <span><b>1363</b>Tourist helpline (English)</span> </span>": "<b>紧急电话</b>（在印度用任何电话均可免费拨打）：<span class=\"sos-grid\"> <span><b>112</b>所有紧急情况</span> <span><b>100</b>报警</span> <span><b>108</b>救护车</span> <span><b>1363</b>旅游求助热线（英语）</span> </span>",
"Within <b>72 hours before landing</b>, also fill in the free <b>India e-Arrival Card</b> online and keep the QR code for immigration. <a href=\"https://indianvisaonline.gov.in/earrival/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">e-Arrival Card →</a>": "<b>在落地前72小时内</b>，请同时在网上填写免费的<b>印度电子入境卡 (e-Arrival Card)</b>，并保存二维码，以便入境检查时出示。<a href=\"https://indianvisaonline.gov.in/earrival/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">电子入境卡 →</a>",
"<a href=\"https://www.hitched.co.uk/wedding-planning/bridalwear-articles/what-to-wear-indian-wedding/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">What to wear to an Indian wedding</a><span>Hitched — written for first-time guests</span>": "<a href=\"https://www.hitched.co.uk/wedding-planning/bridalwear-articles/what-to-wear-indian-wedding/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">参加印度婚礼该穿什么</a><span>Hitched — 专为初次参加的宾客撰写</span>",
"Your presence at our wedding is the greatest gift of all — truly, no gift is expected. If you would still like to bless us with something, here is how, whether you're travelling from overseas or joining us from India.": "您能出席我们的婚礼，就是最珍贵的礼物——真的，无需准备任何礼物。如果您仍想送上祝福，无论您是从海外远道而来，还是在印度与我们相聚，以下方式供您参考。",
"<a href=\"https://vizagpellipoolajada.com/what-to-wear-in-a-south-indian-wedding/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">What to wear in a South Indian wedding: a complete guide</a><span>Vizag Pellipoolajada</span>": "<a href=\"https://vizagpellipoolajada.com/what-to-wear-in-a-south-indian-wedding/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">参加南印度婚礼穿什么：完整指南</a><span>Vizag Pellipoolajada</span>",
